# Where the reader's own copy of the case lives. Kept beside the repository rather
# than in it, so a reader edits one file and touches no spec.
#
# It used to hold real items and real borrowers, and this pointer existed to keep them
# out of git. It does not any more: a case describes the problem and uses invented
# examples, and the records live in the application's own data file. The guard that
# matters now is scripts/no-records-in-repo.py, which refuses a commit carrying records
# in any form.
#
# The form ships blank as CASE.md beside this file. The filled copy is local
# data: it names real people, and it is never committed to this repository or
# to any repository this one becomes. The structural part is the path, not a
# rule: the answers sit outside the worktree, where no git command run inside
# the worktree can reach them. The script at scripts/pre-commit is the second
# control, for the content rather than the file, and scripts/README.md says why
# neither one is a Gate.
#
# A reader edits BANG_CASE_FILE and nothing else. No spec, no registry.

BANG_CASE_DIR=${BANG_CASE_DIR:-$HOME/bang/case}
BANG_CASE_FILE=${BANG_CASE_FILE:-$BANG_CASE_DIR/CASE.md}
BANG_CASE_DATA=${BANG_CASE_DATA:-$BANG_CASE_DIR/data}
